---
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { COMPANY } from "../../data/company";
import { legalHref } from "../../i18n";
---

<LegalPage lang="en" page="cookies">
  <p>
    This policy explains which cookies and similar technologies are used on <strong>{COMPANY.domain}</strong>,
    operated by {COMPANY.name}, and how you can give or withdraw your consent.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-are-cookies">1. What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small files that a website saves in your browser. Some are needed for the website to work, others
    help measure visits. Your browser's local storage (localStorage) works in a similar way, and this policy treats
    it the same.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-use">2. What we use</h2>
  <p>
    We only use two categories: one strictly necessary item that remembers your choice, and Google Analytics
    statistics cookies, which only start if you accept them. We do not use advertising cookies and we do not track
    you across other websites.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Name</th>
          <th scope="col">Category</th>
          <th scope="col">Provider</th>
          <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
          <th scope="col">Duration</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>horelink-consent</code></td>
          <td>Strictly necessary (local storage)</td>
          <td>HoreLink</td>
          <td>Remembers whether you accepted or declined statistics cookies.</td>
          <td>6 months</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_ga</code></td>
          <td>Statistics, consent only</td>
          <td>Google Analytics</td>
          <td>Tells visitors apart, without identifying them.</td>
          <td>2 years</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Statistics, consent only</td>
          <td>Google Analytics</td>
          <td>Keeps the state of the visit session.</td>
          <td>2 years</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    The strictly necessary item does not require your consent, because without it we could not respect the choice
    you made. Google Analytics cookies are not created, and the Google script is not loaded, until you press
    “Accept”.
  </p>

  <h2 id="consent">3. How to give or withdraw consent</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>On your first visit a banner lets you choose “Accept” or “Decline”.</li>
    <li>
      You can change your choice at any time from the “Cookie settings” link in the website footer. If you decline
      after accepting, we delete the Google Analytics cookies set by the website.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can delete or block cookies in your browser settings. If you clear the website's data, the banner will
      appear again.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can block Google Analytics on all websites with Google's official browser add-on
      (<a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a>).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="other-services">4. Links to other services</h2>
  <p>
    When you follow the links to Google Play, the App Store or WhatsApp, you leave our website. Those services may
    use their own cookies under their own policies, which we do not control.
  </p>

  <h2 id="personal-data">5. Personal data</h2>
  <p>
    How we process data obtained through Google Analytics and the contact form is explained in our{" "}
    <a href={legalHref("confidentialitate", "en")}>Privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">6. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about cookies, write to <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
